Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: pass RGB connector bit depth to the VOP

The A12 panel advertises six bits per component. Without output_bpc the
VOP defaults to ten and disables the RGB888-to-RGB666 dithering selected
by the working KNULLI VOP driver. Preserve the connector's bit depth.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_rgb.c
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@
 	}
 
 	s->output_type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_LVDS;
+	s->output_bpc = info->bpc;
 
 	return 0;
 }
